[size=5]Mantis Blades that feel like the Byakko[/size]

The Byakko is Wakako Okada's katana, and it is the best-feeling melee weapon in the game. What makes it feel that way is its loop. You kill someone and the weapon pays you back straight away: a burst of speed, and the stutter between light attacks disappears. You chain into the next target and keep it going.

Mantis Blades are the most cyberpunk weapon in the game and they feel heavy and slow. Killing someone with them gives you nothing.

This mod gives them that loop.

[line]

[size=4]What it does[/size]

[b]Always, while the blades are equipped[/b]
[list]
[*]+1 metre reach
[*]A leap at enemies, including in mid-air
[*]The Byakko's bleed application rate
[*]+25% armour penetration
[*]Attack speed no longer sags as stamina drains
[*]Resting attack speed brought up to 2.1, the Byakko's number
[/list]

[b]On a kill with the blades[/b]
[list]
[*]A burst of attack speed, +17.5% by default, for 10 seconds
[*]The pause between light attack combos is removed for that window
[*]Killing again inside the window starts it over, so a good fight never drops out of it
[/list]

All of it is adjustable in the settings menu, and the defaults are the Byakko's own numbers, so you do not have to configure anything.

[line]

[size=4]You do not need a cap fix mod[/size]

Every other melee attack speed mod warns you about the vanilla 200% melee attack speed ceiling, so this is worth explaining.

The ceiling is real. Bonuses past it still show up on your perks, cyberware and weapon stats and do nothing at all. It does not bite here for two reasons. Most builds have headroom under it, so the burst has somewhere to go. And the half of the effect you feel most is the combo-pause removal, which works through the animation state machine and never goes near the attack speed stat, so no ceiling applies to it.

If your build genuinely is at the ceiling, the speed half of the burst is the only part that loses anything, and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/34588]Melee Attack Speed Cap Fix[/url] resolves it. Press F8 and the mod will tell you whether that is you.

[line]

[size=4]Diagnostics[/size]

Equip the Mantis Blades and press [b]F8[/b] (rebindable). The mod prints what the game actually reports, on screen and into your logs:

[list]
[*]Both attack speed stats, the one the swing animation reads and the one the inventory screen shows. They are separate fields.
[*]Whether each data-layer change landed. A line reading 0 means another Mantis Blade mod replaced the same data.
[*]Whether you are over the vanilla melee cap.
[*]Whether a burst is live, how long it has left, and how many kills you have chained into it.
[/list]

If you are reporting a problem, press F8 and include that readout. It answers most questions before they need asking.

[line]

[size=4]Requirements[/size]

[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/2380]RED4ext[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/1511]redscript[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4197]TweakXL[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/7780]Codeware[/url]
[/list]

[b]Optional:[/b] [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4885]Mod Settings[/url]. Without it the mod runs on its defaults, which are the Byakko's own numbers, and there is simply no menu to change them. Nothing breaks.

[line]

[size=4]Installing and uninstalling[/size]

Install with Vortex as normal, or extract into your Cyberpunk 2077 folder, the one containing bin, r6 and engine. You should end up with [b]r6/scripts/Byakko[/b] and [b]r6/tweaks/Byakko[/b].

To uninstall, delete those two folders. Nothing is written into your save, so there is nothing to clean up and no safe-uninstall procedure to follow. Your character is exactly as it was.

[line]

[size=4]Compatibility[/size]

This mod adds to the Mantis Blade records instead of overwriting them, so another Mantis Blade mod's changes survive alongside it. Where you both change the same stat, both apply. If two mods set the same stat to different absolute values, whichever loads last wins, and F8 will show you if this mod's data layer is being overridden.

Mods covering similar ground, worth a look:
[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/28451]Fenix Mantis Blades - Overhaul[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/34907]Iconic MaxTac Mantis Blades[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/32588]Iconic Mantis Blade[/url]
[/list]

[line]

[size=4]Safety[/size]

Built so it cannot corrupt a save or leave anything behind.

[list]
[*][b]It persists nothing.[/b] No save data, no schema, no migration. Everything it does is a stat modifier on a weapon that only exists while the blades are drawn.
[*][b]It cannot stack.[/b] The burst keeps one modifier per stat at a time, tracked by handle. Killing again pushes the window's deadline out instead of adding a second buff.
[*][b]It stands down during loads, fast travel, time skips, the ripperdoc chair, menus and cutscenes.[/b] That is when the game is rebuilding the world, and reading equipment mid-rebuild is how a mod crashes the game.
[*][b]It does not hook V's damage path.[/b] Kill detection runs on the enemy that died rather than on every hit V deals.
[*][b]A missing optional dependency will not break your other mods.[/b] When a redscript mod references something that is not there, the whole redscript compile fails and every script mod in your game stops working. Every call this mod makes into Mod Settings is isolated so that cannot happen, and all four dependency combinations are checked at build time.
[/list]

[line]

[size=4]Known limits[/size]

[b]Base damage is left alone.[/b] The Byakko's sheet lists 148, but Mantis Blades scale their damage with your level and tier. Pinning them to the katana's number would be a straight downgrade on a Tier 5++ character.

[b]Arm cyberware has a history of ignoring attack speed.[/b] There is a long-standing vanilla bug where arm cyberware and base fists do not scale with attack speed, and how much of it is live varies by patch. This mod is built so that does not matter: the combo-pause removal changes the feel through the animation state machine rather than the attack speed stat, and the speed multiplier is applied to both the blades and V because which one the animation reads has changed between patches.

[line]

Source and issues: [url=https://github.com/tfthushaar/Mantis-Blades-Byakko]github.com/tfthushaar/Mantis-Blades-Byakko[/url]
